  "finalText": "I built the 6-second seamless ambient loop on the **Main** composition (1920×1080, 30 fps). The critique scores it 100/100 with no issues, and the frames at 0 s and 5.97 s match the 0 s frame, so the loop wraps without a visible jump.\n\n- **Background**: a flat deep navy (`#0b0716`) so the colours read as light.\n- **Blobs**: four soft radial-gradient orbs in purple (`#7c3aed`), violet (`#a855f7`), teal (`#14b8a6`) and cyan-teal (`#2dd4bf`). Each drifts about 100–150 px between two positions with Sine In Out easing, and the keys are cycled so the motion returns to its start exactly at 6 s.\n- **Dot grid**: 72 small white dots (8 px) in a 12×6 grid, 120 px apart. Each dot's opacity follows a sine with a 6 s period, phased by its layer index, so a soft ripple moves across the grid and repeats cleanly.\n\nThe blobs are kept at low opacity (40–55%) and the dots at a 8–52% opacity range, so the piece stays calm. If you want the dots more visible on a projector, or the blobs drifting more or less, I can adjust either."
